  "thread": "sam: quick accessibility run on dashboard v2 \u2014 a few small but important nits I hit during keyboard + NVDA testing earlier :mag:\nsam: 1) legend items on the model-comparison chart aren't announced as buttons; NVDA says \"graphic\" and then just lists labels, so you can't toggle series with keyboard\nsam: 2) pagination controls (prev/next) lose focus after click when using enter; focus goes to body and SR reads nothing \u2014 seems like we rerender the whole list without restoring focus\nsam: 3) in dark theme the primary CTA uses #1a73e8 on bg #0b1220 and fails AA contrast at 14px, looks fine visually but flagged by axe\nsam: 4) the filter chip has `aria-pressed` but also `role=\\\"checkbox\\\"` which is redundant and confuses VoiceOver\nsam: filing these here before I make PRs\n\nanya: thanks \u2014 can you add the DOM snippets you saw? especially the legend markup\n\nsam: legend snippet:\n```\n<div class=\"legend-item\"> \n  <span class=\"color-swatch\" style=\"background:#FF6B6B\"></span>\n  <span class=\"label\">Response time</span>\n</div>\n```\nsam: no keyboard handlers and not focusable. I think these should be `<button aria-pressed>` so toggling is reachable and SR-friendly\n\nfrank: agreed. for charts we usually put `role=\\\"group\\\" aria-label=\\\"Legend\\\"` and then make each item a `button` with `aria-pressed` reflecting series visibility. that pattern worked for the heatmap legend we shipped last quarter\n\nluisa: pagination bug: probably because we re-render the list and React unmounts the focused button. easiest fix is to call `nextBtn.focus()` in the callback after state updates or use `id` stable keys and `useEffect` to restore focus by tracking `lastClickedPagination`. also add `aria-live=\\\"polite\\\"` update like \"page 3 of 12\"\n\nsam: good call on aria-live. I'll wire `aria-live` to the page indicator only (avoid noisy announcements on incremental loads).\n\nfrank: contrast: if we bump CTA to #1E86FF it should pass AA. we should also add a dark-theme token `--primary-on-dark` and run theme visual diff tests. luisa can you include this in theme tokens PR?\n\nluisa: yep \u2014 will add token and update storybook snapshots. also will run axe/pa11y against dark theme preview.\na11y-bot: automated scan summary (dashboard-v2/preview): 5 issues (1 high: non-interactive legend items not keyboard accessible; 1 medium: contrast fail on primary btn in dark). Report: https://ci.redwood/axe/scan/3490\n\nsam: priority list from my side: legend keyboard + pagination focus restore + contrast token + chip role cleanup + aria-live for page indicator.\n\nanya: assigning: sam -> legend + chip; luisa -> contrast token + storybook; frank -> pagination focus logic + aria-live. i'll create tickets and add acceptance criteria (keyboard nav steps, SR announcement expectations, axe pass).\n\nfrank: I'll add a tiny e2e that tabs into the chart legend, toggles a series with Space, and asserts SR-visible text changes (and that focus remains on the toggled button). also test pagination focus retention.\n\nluisa: estimate: legend + chip fix (1 day), pagination + e2e (1.5 days), theme token (0.5 day). will queue for next sprint.\n\nsam: thanks \u2014 i'll start the PR draft for legend pattern and include note about not relying on click-only handlers. tagging `@eng-accessibility` when ready. :thumbsup:\n\nanya: cool, please link the axe scan and include steps to repro in the PR description. closing the thread when PRs are up."
